Phase 5 — Linux Security Checks

Check SSH root login configuration

sudo grep PermitRootLogin /etc/ssh/sshd_config

Check if SSH is enabled

sudo systemctl is-enabled ssh

Check if SSH is active

sudo systemctl is-active ssh

List currently running services

sudo systemctl list-units –type=service –state=running

Check for world-writable files directly under /etc

sudo find /etc -maxdepth 1 -type f -perm -002 -ls

Test access with an incorrect username

sudo -u saleuder ls /opt/company/IT

Test access with salesuser

sudo -u salesuser ls /opt/company/IT

Troubleshooting: incorrect usermod command

sudo usermd -aG IT salesuser

Find the correct usermod path

which usermod

Add salesuser to the IT group using the correct path

sudo /usr/sbin/usermod -aG IT salesuser

Verify salesuser group membership

id salesuser